  "scientific_synthesis": [
    "Source-balanced selection improves the fixed k-center comparison in this completed panel: quota k-center reaches19.521558% versus17.843477% for visual k-center, with a1.678081pp regional difference,20/24 positive regions, and a positive leave-one-region-out range.",
    "Geographic weighting also improves a different coverage objective: real source-mean weighted facility location reaches21.239213% versus19.888857% for ordinary FL, and exceeds its size/weight-multiset-preserving permuted control by2.131675pp.",
    "Strong simple baselines sharpen the practical finding: quota random has the highest full-recipe mean(21.413468%); it exceeds quota k-center by1.891909pp. Thus metadata balancing is practically useful here, while greedy farthest-first scoring is not the best observed rule.",
    "At exactly2,300,000 available unique processed training labels per fit, quota k-center versus visual k-center remains positive(+1.996366pp). Its paired change from full labels is+0.318285pp with CI[-0.134505,0.739344].",
    "Under the same pixel control, quota k-center versus permuted groups falls from+0.896339 to+0.246740pp; the directly paired contrast change is-0.649598pp with CI[-1.048668,-0.258262]. This is evidence that the two comparisons respond differently to supervision matching, and motivates joint reporting of source-group semantics and label availability.",
    "The frozen DINOv2-MLP recipe shows its largest quota-k-center versus visual-k-center mean effects atB12(+0.902370pp balanced,+1.332156pp skewed), with smaller differences atB24(+0.167843,+0.319785) and mixed B6 directions(-0.240052,+0.165535).",
    "All ten matched B12/skewed strategy means are higher for the frozen DINOv2-MLP recipe than for the full ResNet18 U-Net-style recipe(by4.401640 to7.057375pp). This comparison concerns the complete recipes, which differ in representation, architecture and supervision."
  ],
  "contribution_assessment": {
    "assessment": "The completed evidence supports a substantive controlled empirical contribution: it identifies when source-group balancing helps visual subset selection, compares hard quotas with source-mean coverage weights under the same feature information, and shows which contrasts persist under equal available processed-label budgets.",
    "recommended_central_claim": "Source-group balancing can improve unseen-region segmentation under limited image budgets; its value depends on the coverage objective, supervision budget and model recipe.",
    "distinctive_evidence_chain": [
      "Exact same-pool image-budget comparisons with group-size-preserving and weight-multiset-preserving geographic controls.",
      "A complete576-fit logical matrix evaluated on24 fixed new regions, with allocation/seed averaging before geographic inference.",
      "A matched27-fit available-pixel intervention and direct paired regional changes, separating robustness to label quantity from image-count comparisons.",
      "A complementary frozen-representation recipe spanning two pool profiles and three budgets."
    ],
